  "description": "§27e: an open door stops occluding §27's rays. Four arms over one wooden door in a wall gap, midnight, one torch. Arm 2 is the control -- opening the door with the flag off must reproduce arm 1 exactly, because vanilla's glow grid never learns a door opened. Arms 3 and 4 draw the SAME polygon and differ only in whether vanilla's gameplay light is moved to match, which is why door_outside_ground_glow is pinned next to every vector_light_* probe: it is the only number that can tell the drawn-only divergence from the coherent one.",
