    {
      "type": "SetFeature",
      "args": {
        "featureName": "vector_lights",
        "enabled": "true"
      },
      "description": "THE SHIPPED DEFAULT, and the one arm here that lets the clock run. With leaf tracking on, the glow-grid hole is not opened by the notification -- it is opened by GameComponent_DoorAperture when the leaves finish sliding. Nothing above can test that, because a paused scenario never advances OpenPct. This arm opens the door with the clock running, waits out the swing, and then asks vanilla's own gameplay light whether the doorway became a hole."
    },
    {
      "type": "SetFeature",
      "args": {
        "featureName": "vector_light_penumbra",
        "enabled": "true"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "SetFeature",
      "args": {
        "featureName": "vector_light_suppress",
        "enabled": "true"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "SetFeature",
      "args": {
        "featureName": "vector_light_blend",
        "enabled": "true"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "SetFeature",
      "args": {
        "featureName": "vector_light_mask",
        "enabled": "true"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "SetFeature",
