        "enabled": "true"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "SetFeature",
      "args": {
        "featureName": "vector_light_door_glow_blocker",
        "enabled": "true"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "SetFeature",
      "args": {
        "featureName": "vector_light_door_aperture",
        "enabled": "true"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "SetDoorOpen",
      "args": {
        "offset": "0,45",
        "open": "false"
      },
      "description": "Shut first, so the swing this arm measures is a real one from zero."
    },
    {
      "type": "SetTimeSpeed",
      "args": {
        "speed": "normal"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "SetDoorOpen",
      "args": {
        "offset": "0,45",
        "open": "true"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Wait",
      "args": {
        "frames": "60"
      },
      "description": "Long enough for the leaves to finish: a wooden door slides in well under 60 ticks, and the same 60 is what vector_light_door_close uses to settle a swing."
    },
    {
      "type": "SetTimeSpeed",
      "args": {
        "speed": "paused"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "door_outside_ground_glow",
        "expectedValue": "0.5",
        "tolerance": "0.005"
      },
      "description": "THE ASSERTION. Vanilla's own GroundGlowAt beyond a FULLY SLID door. 0.0951 is what a blocked doorway delivers here and 0.5 is what a hole in the wall does, so this separates 'the bit moved' from 'the bit never moved' by a factor of five rather than by a tolerance."
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "door_inside_ground_glow",
        "expectedValue": "0.5",
        "tolerance": "0.005"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Screenshot",
      "args": {
        "fileName": "opendoor_tracked_open_glowgrid.png"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "SetTimeSpeed",
      "args": {
        "speed": "normal"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "SetDoorOpen",
      "args": {
        "offset": "0,45",
        "open": "false"
      },
      "description": "AND BACK. The bit is restored on the FIRST tick of a close rather than at the end of one, so this also pins that a door told to shut stops being a hole immediately -- the asymmetry DoorApertureMath.GlowGridHoleWanted describes."
    },
    {
      "type": "Wait",
      "args": {
        "frames": "60"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "SetTimeSpeed",
      "args": {
        "speed": "paused"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "door_outside_ground_glow",
        "expectedValue": "0.0951154977",
        "tolerance": "0.005"
      },
      "description": "Back to exactly what a shut door delivers: turning the door back into a blocker has to restore vanilla, not leave the hole standing."
    },
    {
      "type": "Screenshot",
      "args": {
        "fileName": "opendoor_tracked_shut_glowgrid.png"
      }
    }
